<title>PORTUGAL: EIB issues 20 bln esc 10-yr Navigator 3-mth Lisbor.</title>
<headline>EIB issues 20 bln esc 10-yr Navigator 3-mth Lisbor.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Investment Bank (EIB) is issuing a 20 billion escudo 10-year variable rate Navigator bond indexed to three-month Lisbor &quot;flat&quot; with a &quot;cap&quot; of 9.25 percent, the leaders of the operation said.</p>
<p>The leaders are Banco Cisf, Banco Portugues de Investimento and Caixa Geral de Depositos.  </p>
<p>ISSUER: European Investment Bank</p>
<p>TYPE: Variable rate bonds</p>
<p>RATING: AAA (Standard &amp; Poor's); Aaa (Moody's)</p>
<p>AMOUNT: 20 billion escudos</p>
<p>INTEREST RATE: 3-mth Lisbor subject to 9.25 pct &quot;cap&quot;</p>
<p>PAYMENT OF INTEREST: March 15, June 15, Sept 15, Dec 15</p>
<p>MATURITY: 15 Dec 2006</p>
<p>DATE OF ISSUE: 16 Dec 1996</p>
<p>ISSUE PRICE: 100.125 percent</p>
<p>COMMISSIONS: 0.23 percent</p>
<p>ADMISSION TO: Luxembourg bourse</p>
<p>LEAD MANAGERS AND BOOKRUNNERS: Cisf, BPI, CGD</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +(351-1) 3538254</p>
</text>
